"subs": [
{
"t": 0.0,
"dur": 2.101,
"text": "…four hundred twelve. Four hundred thirteen."
},
{
"t": 2.401,
"dur": 9.774,
"text": "Nobody opened it for three generations. The family was the richest on the block for three generations. To Mr. Khai, the jar could only hold gold."
},
{
"t": 12.474,
"dur": 6.262,
"text": "Friday night, Mr. Khai took a shovel to the kitchen. He'd grab the gold before handing over the house."
},
{
"t": 18.986,
"dur": 3.261,
"text": "He went into the storage room for a pickaxe. The door shut."
},
{
"t": 22.498,
"dur": 1.563,
"text": "Open up! I own this house!"
},
{
"t": 24.311,
"dur": 5.746,
"text": "I know, sir. Selling a house means taking inventory. Great-great-grandpa said so. I'll count it for you."
},
{
"t": 30.307,
"dur": 2.769,
"text": "…four hundred twelve. Four hundred thirteen. That's all."
},
{
"t": 34.276,
"dur": 4.115,
"text": "Four hundred thirteen what? It's not gold. Full story right below."
}
],
